Capture Cargo oracle metadata and unit graph as a normalized Rust package plan receipt

Usage: mantle rust-plan [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --root <ROOT>
          Rust workspace root (default: current directory)
  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose logging
      --cargo <CARGO>
          Cargo executable to invoke for metadata and unit-graph capture [default: cargo]
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --json
          Emit errors as JSON objects for tooling integration
      --rustc <RUSTC>
          rustc executable to invoke for verbose toolchain identity [default: rustc]
      --compiler-policy-mode <COMPILER_POLICY_MODE>
          Compiler-policy mode for Rust unit execution: plain, audit, deny, or required [default: plain]
      --store <STORE>
          Where to export final build outputs on disk. Intermediate deps stay in castore. Source inputs always come from /nix/store. If not writable, builds still succeed (outputs in castore) [default: /nix/store]
      --compiler-policy-provider-manifest <COMPILER_POLICY_PROVIDER_MANIFEST>
          Compiler-policy provider manifest JSON consumed at the rustc invocation boundary
      --store-prefix <STORE_PREFIX>
          Logical store path prefix for derivation hashes. All output paths and ATerm hashes are computed against this prefix. Default: /mantle/store. Use --nix-compat for /nix/store [default: /mantle/store]
      --compiler-policy-provider-manifest-digest <COMPILER_POLICY_PROVIDER_MANIFEST_DIGEST>
          Expected BLAKE3 digest for the compiler-policy provider manifest
      --nix-compat
          Shorthand for --store-prefix=/nix/store. For interop testing with Nix-computed derivations
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          State directory for pathinfo.redb, blobs, and logs. Default: legacy $CRUNCH_STATE_DIR or $XDG_STATE_HOME/crunch or ~/.local/state/crunch. Use --state-dir for an explicit Mantle path
      --target <TARGETS>
          Target triple to pass to Cargo; repeatable
      --base-store <BASE_STORES>
          Ordered list of read-only base store state directories for overlay composition. Declared in priority order (base A before base B)
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Cargo profile for unit graph capture [default: dev]
      --features <FEATURES>
          Comma-separated features to enable
      --all-features
          Enable all Cargo features
      --no-default-features
          Disable default Cargo features
      --no-cargo-oracle
          Use Mantle's native Rust planner/executor only; do not invoke Cargo as oracle or orchestrator
      --execute-first-supported-unit
          Execute the first supported lib/bin unit from the captured explicit derivation graph
      --execute-first-dependency-chain
          Execute the first bounded dependency chain from the captured explicit derivation graph
      --execute-target-topology
          Execute a bounded target-only unit topology from the captured explicit derivation graph
      --execute-host-artifact-topology
          Execute a bounded host-artifact unit topology from the captured explicit derivation graph
      --execute-topology
          Execute a bounded unified host+target unit topology from the captured explicit derivation graph
      --execute-dev-dependency-test-topology
          Execute a bounded native dev-dependency test topology from explicit receipts
      --execute-workspace-dependency-topology
          Execute a bounded native workspace-dependency topology from explicit receipts
      --execute-patch-source-topology
          Execute a bounded native patch-source topology from explicit receipts
      --execution-output-root <EXECUTION_OUTPUT_ROOT>
          Output directory for execution artifacts
      --local-rust-cache <LOCAL_RUST_CACHE>
          Explicit local Rust unit cache policy [default: off] [possible values: off, read, read-write]
      --shared-rust-cache <SHARED_RUST_CACHE>
          Explicit shared Rust unit cache policy [default: off] [possible values: off, read, read-write]
      --shared-rust-cache-source <SHARED_RUST_CACHE_SOURCES>
          Ordered shared Rust result source: an HTTP(S) base URL or directory
      --shared-rust-cache-publish-target <SHARED_RUST_CACHE_PUBLISH_TARGET>
          Shared Rust publication target: an HTTP(S) base URL or directory
      --shared-rust-cache-trusted-key <SHARED_RUST_CACHE_TRUSTED_KEYS>
          Trusted shared Rust verifier in name:base64 format; repeatable
      --shared-rust-cache-producer-policy <SHARED_RUST_CACHE_PRODUCER_POLICIES>
          Accepted shared Rust producer-policy identity; repeatable
      --shared-rust-cache-signing-key <SHARED_RUST_CACHE_SIGNING_KEY>
          Nix-format Ed25519 key file for shared Rust result publication
      --shared-rust-cache-offline
          Keep remote shared Rust result and object sources unopened
  -h, --help
          Print help
